import Submission.Work.XHostT.TDef

/-!
# (key: bridge-host-cross) The route of ONE call of the cross-replica hosted network

For the call `(ρ, l)` at global time `τ = tm ρ l`:
* `adaptT τ`: the free adapters of time `τ` on ALL roles (every host chain of every replica `Hb → Hp`, every bank
  `Zb → Zp`): `Ffr τ → Afr τ`;
* `stage<l>`: Shea's stage `l` (pair `pairL l` of replica `ρ`) with its slots on banks or on idle data roles of ANY
  replica (TRoles' `ghliftT`); the hosted roles take the residual `Wn`, every other host chain and bank moves to
  time `τ + 1`: `Afr τ → Bfr ρ l`;
* `tail<l>`: the remaining climbs of ρ's windows that end at stage `l` and Shea's gate layers, on ρ's run only
  (`liftT_route`): `Bfr ρ l → Ffr (τ + 1)`;
* `call<l>`: the three, with the scalar map `liftRunT ρ (runMap l)` and the price `|Γ| * callU ρ l`.
Ryan Shea's complex588 tree (Bridge401: Nil Mamano's gen401 on Dugongue #401 / jacklightChen #377 / Lydakis #275 / DaysSky #363; engine and E8 unit by Jacob Sussman), DaysSky's idle-axis hosting (CrocSwap/integer-mult-bounds PR #442), h-L3-build / fsp-perrun / lg-a2a4 (wht43).  Generated by p-a3/tools/gen_xnet.py (wht45/lever, 19 Oct 2026); prepared with assistance from Claude.  No `sorry`.
-/

set_option linter.unusedSectionVars false
